# A small, curated snapshot of the *actual* describing triples for the DPV
# (Data Privacy Vocabulary) terms tests/data/problem/valid/
# HealthDataset-shacl-full.yaml references -- fetched and checked directly
# against DPV's own real turtle source on 2026-08-25, not assumed or
# invented. Loaded into test_dataset_conforms_to_real_healthdcat_ap_shacl's
# validation call (merged into the data graph) so pyshacl's sh:class checks
# have the real membership triples to check against, instead of failing
# simply because the bare term reference in our own instance data carries no
# local proof of it.
#
# DPV-only now: the EU Publications Office / HealthDCAT-AP-specific terms
# this file used to also carry (data-theme/HEAL, access-right/NON_PUBLIC,
# frequency/ANNUAL, language/ENG) are superseded as of 2026-08-26 by
# test_shacl_validation.py's own _official_vocabulary_catalogue_graph(),
# which loads the same real, populated vocabulary catalogue Sciensano's
# official hosted validator preloads -- more complete and more authoritative
# than this hand-picked snippet ever was for anything HealthDCAT-AP's own
# MDR-managed authority tables cover. DPV isn't one of those tables (it's a
# separate w3id.org ontology), so it still needs its own snapshot here.
#
# Deliberately a static, checked-in snapshot, not a live fetch during test
# runs: this project already has direct, confirmed evidence that w3id.org's
# own permalink redirects are intermittently flaky (see
# docs/architecture-verification.md), and a live network dependency inside
# a test that's supposed to be a fast, deterministic regression check is
# the same class of risk, just against a different host.

@prefix skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#> .
@prefix dpv: <https://w3id.org/dpv#> .
@prefix dpvpd: <https://w3id.org/dpv/dpv-pd#> .
@prefix dct: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

dpv:LegalObligation
    a skos:Concept, dpv:LegalBasis .

dpv:ScientificResearch
    a skos:Concept, dpv:Purpose .

# Not DPV's own triples, unlike the two above: HealthDCAT-AP release 8 requires
# dpv:hasPersonalData values to match ^https://w3id.org/dpv/dpv-pd#.+ and its
# own example types such terms inline as `dpvpd:Age a dpv:PersonalData`, which
# is all this does for the fixture's term. DPV 2.3 itself defines its
# personal-data categories under https://w3id.org/dpv/pd# (checked 2026-10-21),
# e.g. pd:MedicalHealth, so this IRI is the official profile's convention, not a
# DPV term -- see the fixture's own comment.
dpvpd:MedicalHealth
    a dpv:PersonalData .

# Also not a DPV triple: the EU Publications Office frequency catalogue
# (frequencies.rdf in the official validator's catalogue) declares its terms
# as skos:Concept only, while the official shape for cv:frequency checks
# sh:class dct:Frequency. The official example types the terms it uses inline
# (`<.../frequency/DAILY> a dct:Frequency`, at its end); the fixture's
# opening hours use DAILY, so it is typed the same way here.
<http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/frequency/DAILY>
    a dct:Frequency .
